From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] camel: include glib.h when S/MIME is disabled

camel_smime_context_util_nss_error_to_string() sits after the
#endif /* ENABLE_SMIME */ that closes the block starting at the top of the
file, and that block holds every #include, glib's among them. Its signature
uses glib types, so a build without S/MIME has nothing declaring them:

  camel-smime-context.c:1911:7: error: unknown type name 'gchar'
  camel-smime-context.c:1912:47: error: unknown type name 'gint'

The function is meant to be built either way - it returns NULL when S/MIME is
off, and says so in its own documentation - so include glib.h outside the
guard.

Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/src/camel/camel-smime-context.c
+++ b/src/camel/camel-smime-context.c
@@ -25,6 +25,8 @@
 
 #include "evolution-data-server-config.h"
 
+#include <glib.h>
+
 #ifdef ENABLE_SMIME
 
 #include "nss.h"
